[dopamine] VERDICT: BOUNDARY
BOUNDARY -- OBJREL did not recover 6-seed-blind (5/6 overall, 2/3 blind; need >=5/6 AND all blind) -- reward-modulated salience-weighted plasticity ALSO does not reach the minority signed direction on this substrate (objrel-slot0 mean 0.83); the plasticity is INERT / does no real work (PRE-learning objrel-slot0 0.17 already ~= learned 0.83) -- NOT a real emergent result; REWARD is NOT load-bearing (no-reward 0.17 / shuffled 0.00 recover ~as well as reward-on 0.83 -- the DA signal is not what drives it); SALIENCE is NOT load-bearing (uniform non-salience reward 0.83 recovers ~as well as salience-weighted 0.83, OR both fail -- the salience weighting is not the escape mechanism). THE PRECISE FRONTIER (load-bearing): the Dale-LEGAL signed spiking read EXISTS in weight space (the ANALYTIC Dale reference reads canonical 1.00 AND objrel-slot0 1.00 GENUINELY ON SPIKES + Dale-legal), and the reservoir FEATURE robustly encodes objrel (a HOST linear argmax generalizes it held-out ~100%) -- so this is NOT the substrate/representation/Dale's-law wall. The residual is EMERGENT REACHABILITY of a minority signed direction under a 7:1 class imbalance: dopamine-gated three-factor plasticity with salience-weighted DA reaches objrel-slot0 0.83 (vs the fixed-WTA 0.50, vs the analytic target 1.00). These numbers characterize EXACTLY how far a biologically-grounded reward-modulated (striatal) rule with a salience prior carries the emergent learning, GENUINELY ON SPIKES + Dale-LEGAL + NOT ridge-warm-started (the emergent constraint honored). An HONEST characterization; NO anti-cheat was weakened to force a GO.
